    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the offensive charge with an elite efficiency score of 87.14. Facing Tomoyuki Sugano (5.02 xERA), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive platoon advantage and an optimal #2 spot in the order, making him our primary engine for R/RBI production. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) follow as our next highest-rated plays; both take advantage of soft matchups against struggling starters, with **Tyler Soderstrom** specifically benefiting from a favorable ballpark environment against Nick Martinez, while **Gabriel Moreno** anchors the lineup with high-contact expectations against Sugano.\n\nThe optimizer leaned heavily into park and platoon efficiency, which pushed **Max Muncy** (61.22) and **Henry Bolte** (59.91) into the lineup despite lower baseline projections. **Max Muncy** is buoyed by a +10% park factor and the expectation that he can exploit Nick Martinez\u2019s high xERA, even hitting from the #8 hole. Conversely, the toughest call of the morning was benching **Jose Caballero** (43.67). While he offers elite SB upside and a positive indicator from a slow-delivering pitcher, his poor platoon split against Bryan Woo ultimately capped his potential, leaving him just short of the 45-point threshold required to displace players like **Cole Young** (45.30) or **Austin Riley** (47.47). \n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as official confirmation for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Brice Turang** remains critical to these projected efficiencies. While we like the matchup for **Isaac Paredes** (62.81) given the wind blowing out, we remain cautious regarding **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young**, as both face a more difficult arm in Ryan Weathers (3.41 xERA). We remain without the services of **James Wood**, who continues to sit on the IL, while our other high-upside bench depth including **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Edwin Arroyo** are held in reserve to ensure we do not hit our daily game cap prematurely in what looks like a high-scoring day for the squad.",
